`BaseOptimizer.apply()` takes the branch that builds the optimizer on the first call when `trainable_variables` are passed and `self.built` is false. For `SGD`, `build()` first calls `super().build(variables)`, then, because `momentum=0.5` is nonzero, it loops over every variable and appends `self.add_variable_from_reference(..., name="momentum")` once per variable. The test passes 7 variables, so `add_variable_from_reference` is called 7 times.

